WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.238
Unit 1 is what the runbook adds.

2
00:00:02.238 --> 00:00:06.097
One settings file per stage holds
every value the commands need,

3
00:00:06.097 --> 00:00:10.175
and the settings reader enforces
its rules before any command runs.

4
00:00:10.175 --> 00:00:14.993
No secrets: a secret-like name, such
as password, client secret or token,

5
00:00:14.993 --> 00:00:18.544
with a value, stops the run,
and the ServiceNow token

6
00:00:18.544 --> 00:00:21.925
is read at run time from
an environment variable.

7
00:00:21.925 --> 00:00:24.563
No placeholders in an enabled provider.

8
00:00:24.563 --> 00:00:27.624
The stage it says it is,
checked by the pre-flight.

9
00:00:27.624 --> 00:00:30.962
And named notice contacts
for each enabled provider.

10
00:00:30.962 --> 00:00:32.975
Every collector call is a read.

11
00:00:32.975 --> 00:00:35.941
The kit's writes are
few, and each is gated:

12
00:00:35.941 --> 00:00:40.885
the Azure Policy assignment and
its remediation, and the rollback,

13
00:00:40.885 --> 00:00:44.570
run only with apply and the
plan's approved SHA-256;

14
00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:49.963
payloads go to the agency's endpoint
only with send and the settings flag.

15
00:00:49.963 --> 00:00:53.299
The settings file also
names each provider's cloud.

16
00:00:53.299 --> 00:00:58.953
The estate the runbook writes for is
Microsoft 365 G C C with commercial Azure,

17
00:00:58.953 --> 00:01:02.663
on the worldwide Graph and
Resource Manager hosts.

18
00:01:02.663 --> 00:01:06.713
GCC High and DoD are other
names in the same file.

19
00:01:06.713 --> 00:01:10.900
The kit doesn't build the ServiceNow
endpoint; that's the agency's.
